      "body": "fixes #47409\n\n### what changed\nunder attention-dp (`attn_dp_size > 1`), `dp_rank` is `None`:\n1. `SchedulerKvEventsPublisher` hardcoded `dp_rank or 0` for `kv_metrics.data_parallel_rank`, publishing rank 0 across all attention-dp shards and breaking downstream kv-aware router load balancing (e.g. dynamo).\n2. prometheus scheduler series omitted `dp_rank` entirely when `dp_rank is None`, making it impossible to join with radix cache metrics (which use `parallel.attn_dp_rank`).\n\n- use `select_kv_publisher_dp_rank` for `kv_metrics.data_parallel_rank` in `kv_events_publisher.py`\n- populate `labels[\"dp_rank\"] = parallel.attn_dp_rank` when `attn_dp_size > 1` in `metrics_collector.py`\n- added unit tests for `select_kv_publisher_dp_rank` / `emit_kv_metrics` and scheduler metrics labels under attention-dp\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41116646531](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41116646531)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41116645618](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41116645618)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41116645759](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41116645759)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
